CORE smt-backend
main.py
--python-smt-strings --cvc5
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
The refined-string parse intrinsic has no SMT encoding, so with native
strings int() was unconstrained (int("0", 16) == -1 was a counterexample).
The value is now composed from the characters: exact for 1..K digits of
the base, unconstrained for other spellings.
